| Three doors: Edge+Stride, Ward+Sustain, Resilience | `CANON` | All three open at protagonist's Kindling |
| Guard = Stride's second shape | `RESERVED` | Book 2 reveal — do not show in Book 1 |
| Mars disk lineage | `RESERVED` | Never explained. Aria's database match is the closest it gets |
| Two Makers myth | `RESERVED` | Do not reference in Book 1 |
| Failing filter: each generation finds doors more accessible | `CANON` | Background anxiety — older families mistrust new Kindled ease |
| Filter acceleration: the recession rate has increased in the last generation | `CANON` | Homura captain's log establishes this. Implications: RESERVED |
| The EMP (600 years ago) | `CANON` | Severed civilization from its technological base. Recovery took generations |
| 600th anniversary: Year 0 of book takes place on this anniversary | `CANON` | Cultural moment — celebrations across the wormhole network |
| Medical-Ember synthesis: now integrated | `CANON` | Pre-EMP they were separate disciplines. Integration = 400-year project |
| Intergalactic travel: normal infrastructure | `CANON` | Characters may have multi-planet backgrounds |
| Neuro-optic / classification overlay | `CANON` | Standard for training institution practitioners. Combined-path produces anomalous output |
| The Homura: research vessel, Ember-certified crew | `CANON` | Opens the book via captain's log. Destination: RESERVED |
| Combined-path configuration: should not exist at first Kindling | `CANON` | This is the engine of the book |
| The pre-EMP historical case (overlay pattern match) | `RESERVED` | Aria finds the fragmented record. One occurrence. 600 years ago |
| Soul as power-source: Ember and magic share the same brain region | `CANON` | fMRI discovery. The "unused space." Rook saw the images. |
| Rook: historical figure, research subject, founder of Touren lineage | `CANON` | Met his love at the medical research station. Carried the knowledge through the EMP. |
| Rook's disk: now carried by the protagonist | `CANON` | Passed through 600 years of Touren lineage practitioners |
| Touren Academy: chartered institution, Rook's lineage | `CANON` | Teaches unified theory. Rift-awareness in curriculum. |
| Wyck's Academy: chartered institution, parallel lineage | `CANON` | Different methodology, same soul-source truth. Competitive but not hostile |
| Rook's rift-spawn fighters: non-chartered, active | `CANON` | Informal group. Know what the coming fight is. Not warning loudly. |
| The rifts: locations where the barrier thins | `CANON` | Things come through. Rift-spawn fighters handle encounters. |
| Something on the other side of the filter | `RESERVED` | What the disk's fever dream glimpses. Has been waiting. |
| The disk has changed with the magical influx | `POSSIBLE` | How it changed: owner decision. See four POSSIBLE candidates in storyboard. |
| The training's true purpose | `RESERVED` for general population, `CANON` for Touren lineage | Glory = minimum viable for interface with what's on the other side |
| The EMP broke the filter — not damaged, broke | `CANON` | The filter is a literal barrier. The crack has been propagating for 600 years. |
| The filter fully breaks — outcome of the series | `PLANNED` | Book 3 event. Not a question of if, only when. |
| The Glory Realm: populated, competitive, has its own ladder | `CANON` | Glory = their entry point. Past-Glory: RESERVED. Not hostile by default. |
| Other power-filled worlds in the Glory Realm | `CANON` | Have been at Glory-equivalent or above for centuries. They have been waiting. |
| The protagonist's combined-path = Glory-native configuration at Kindled | `CANON` | The series thesis: they begin where the civilization ends up. |
| Past-Glory: the next ladder | `RESERVED` | Structure, bottom rung, ceiling: all RESERVED. Revealed when filter breaks. |

