   278	- Iron Wall's first showing; the records' grade; the reading inward.
   279	
   280	After the first third, progression language surfaces at turning points: the three notices, the grade, the court's line.
   281	**Measurement caution (as OWNER-DECISIONS #14):** the last third carries **grade vocabulary** (first-, second- and third-tier; the mark; the stroke and bar). Counted as progression vocabulary, it inflates the closing third. Report two counts at each review, with and without grade/taxonomy terms.
