series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md:78:**Key scene:** Cael's Kindling. The Arbiter appears, goes silent for 11 seconds (long enough that the certification officer starts to sweat), and resolves to [SHATTERED]. The officer's face. The room clearing. Hesk walking Cael out through the back exit.
series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md:181:**The revelation:** Seln provides his intelligence cache — the files he collected during his years as a Compact operative, which he has been carrying since he walked away from the job. The files confirm: the Guilds Compact has been falsifying Path classifications for two hundred years. Practitioners who develop abilities the Compact finds politically inconvenient are reclassified into lesser Paths at their Kindling evaluation. The falsification is built into the Arbiter evaluation protocol — a modification made so long ago that no current Compact official knows it's there.
series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md:304:**Key scene:** Cael, alone at an Arbiter station, asks his Arbiter — the sigil that has been dark since his Kindling — to tell him what it sees when it evaluates him. The Arbiter activates, for the first time, and says: *I cannot evaluate you. You predate my categories.* Then it goes dark again. This is the first confirmation, from within the system itself, of what the tomb record described.
series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md:389:**Final image:** A child, age 14, somewhere in Valdris. Their Kindling arrives. The Arbiter appears — different now, less rigid, more curious. The classification resolves.
series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md:421:- **What Book 9 inherits:** the court's centre (no edge; "the same kind of made"); the Rune finding nobody else knows; the instruments reading wronger (trend up — Book 11); the Arbiter dark; the crack; Vastin unadmitted; Oryn's route; Teague's next spring; the letter west to Hesk; thirteen fragments; the leaf's copies with the gap drawn; the mule with Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:86:**What the system sees:** [SHATTERED]. The file reads *Active non-compliance. Observation priority escalated.* Asset-restriction is *pending jurisdiction* and executes west of the Line on showing paper. The Suppression-Advisory Watch is at Level 4, unchanged (origin: Book 6's matter; untouched here).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:25:- **Seln (cutaway, Ch18).** Observation, not inference; the colleague ended by one adjective. The first product, true and dry, walked down to the Ostrand courier himself. Gault's four questions. The arithmetic error that settles the office's opinion of him. **Made on day twenty-three** at the empty gallery, and the eleven seconds of being pleased before the thought finished. Made twice before in fifteen years, never by a target. Withdraw, escalate, or keep working: he keeps working. The subject does nothing, and Seln feels *accounted for*. "The interesting question is who taught him to watch."
