editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/AUTHORSHIP.md:23:**Method.** `EVENT-LIST.md` was written first, in my own words, choosing every scene's entry and inventing the mechanics the packet leaves open (the cache's physical contents and texts, the routes, the four findings' evidence, the clean door's sections, the perception session's tests, the borrowed office and the note, Vastin's three refusals' reasoning and his window). Drafting followed the list. After the full draft, rhythm was repaired by reading: every change was a hand-composed exact-string replacement (joining clipped statements that were one thought; no sentence split by script). Scene markers were removed or added by hand at points where the scene was continuous or a time-shift occurred. Canon corrections found on re-reading the edition (the Kindling at Denvash is the practitioner's own Arbiter and a brass plate, not a station frame; the first Wind notice came on a cot at Ardenmere; the B4 minute predates the stair; the stratum line sits in the notebook cover, not on a card) were re-composed by hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/reserved-truths-prompt.md:5:**1. Kindling mechanics (ch35–37, and wherever else they appear).** As drafted in the edition, Kindling is the person's own Arbiter waking and a brass plate lighting.
