editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:1025:Lira saw it too, a step later than he did. She stopped. She stood in a narrowing strip of honest wood with Fiske's slick on both sides of her and across her front, and every inch of the strip had been drawn, in eleven seconds, by a woman who knew exactly where Lira's feet liked to go and had simply removed all of those places before Lira got there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/pre-repair-r2/chapter-20.md:93:Eleven seconds, all of it. While it went by, Cael's mind did a thing it often did in that room and went backward without asking him: to the side door an hour ago, where the young officer with the ruled board had lost his cold, and had not needed to ask the last name on his list because somebody had already copied it into the door log from the last sitting, *Caelen Hesk-ward*, so that all he had to write was the standing, *the enrollee of record, unclassified*, which took him nine seconds now that his hand knew the way. To the long floor, where Cael had crossed *nine*, *ten*, *eleven* and sat down with *seventeen* under his left foot for the third time, and known this time that he had walked to it on purpose. You could not choose the room. You could choose where you stood in it. And further back, to the ferry, where Karis had written one word on a slip and folded it twice and handed it to Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:21:| 6 | The Records Hall | 4,466 | 4 | **The night:** the fire-watch's oil book, *Records hall. Lamps late. On the registrar's authority, and at his charge.* Bracken, Karis (assistant to bed at the tenth bell), Cael, and **the house's counsel** (a steel joiner's rule; eleven years' retainer, name on nothing; distinguished from the inspection's counsel); Withrow coming and going. **Withrow's pocket code:** *at its discretion* underlined twice (black ink, ruled; brown, unruled, nine years on); "A condition is a place you are put"; Bracken counts the dates in chapter fourteen: none. **Cael's tallies:** nineteen leaves, thirty-seven paragraphs, three schedules; nine discretions, three evidences, one fraud in the negative; schedule two in declaration grammar, with *Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4* cited and not argued; an unknown procurator of record; "They expect to be agreed with." **The counsel reads backward**, from the remedy up; four sentences of recital. **The four rulings:** a ferryman's daughter at a southern river house, a mason's apprentice and two older ones, all sustained; plus Greyvane, five. **First finding (Karis):** no fraud. **Second (counsel):** paragraph six concedes the clause ("look at what he has kept"). **Third:** paragraph seven quotes **Vastin's advisory** whole, with approval (B5 ch5 text). Karis knows her own bench sentence in it; **frightened by a citation**; "Minuted." Cael's note on official channels |
