editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3687:- **The circle:** the road east as Lira's sum (the last Arbiter station four days past Ostrand loaded, three light; stamps stop there; two carters go past, the third turns at it and won't say why); the coastal default and *fled*; forty days after the fourth sitting's close; the five offices' inventories closed (Seln); Jent's sentence on the record; the fossil provision's two paragraphs (the second kept unmentioned); the escort order whole; a "facilities office" nobody can place; **Anchor Path** as a name and a use (rare; service; enforcement; holds people) — **inferred only: no range, rate or cost**; the three-way distinction (Ternhall's anchors / the Lattice Path / Anchor Path).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:3997:At age 14, every person undergoes Kindling: the moment their latent Path potential activates. Kindling is involuntary — it happens regardless of whether the person is ready. An **Arbiter** appears at the moment of Kindling: a small glowing sigil that only the Kindling person can see and hear. The Arbiter evaluates the person's internal architecture and assigns their Path classification.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4019:As a practitioner advances through ranks, new abilities manifest — presented by the Arbiter as visible ability declarations, experienced as text-like constructs in the practitioner's perception. These are called **Path declarations** and are specific to the practitioner's Path type.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4127:- **The line is sharp, not a gradient:** a stride inside, the Arbiter is dark and no declaration renders; a stride outside, it is back — practitioners describe the return as a clock resuming (Lira's clock). Every Arbiter in a party fails identically, at the same stride, one way and back the same, regardless of Path or tier (B7 Ch10–11, Ch18, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4256:- **The cache, in order**: reclassification orders clipped to Kindling records (forty; "nine weeks of nothing"; **the river-town father's letter and the clerk's honest four-line answer**); field reports (corrected down, never up); two centuries of memoranda (*corrective classification at Kindling evaluation*; Brom: "That's a form."); the leaf in its sleeve (*advisory corrections function*). Seln's four movements; **the finding said once**; "How many?" / "I stopped estimating."; Lira on what being pleasant cost him; "My mother's ledger was always right."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:4258:- **Two Hundred Years** — Karis's four findings, each landing on a carried thread: the mechanism and **reach, not strength**; the flag as the corrections function failing safe — *"She just never knew what was answering."* (Ilsev and Havel never told, in eleven words); **the strata** — [UNBOUND] said **once**, here only [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: this is the series' second voicing; B4 ch50 voiced the older word once, lower-case, at Halcenvane (Karis, one factual clause), and B5 carries it read-and-closed; this chapter builds on ch50 and does not discover it; audit B5]; *close the door, remove the exit, delete the name*; **the limit, verbatim**; Lira: "They *found* it… It isn't a long time compared to whatever's under it." (a Book 9 plant); the anomaly checked — *Not this either. Still open.*; the stratum note paid (re-evaluation as delivery mechanism); Seln: "A convenience cannot." It can't be filed. "It isn't broken. It's maintained." Lira on the stair: **"It's not evidence. It's a map."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:39:- "four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more had put his turn on the fifth count" (Chapter 52, exchange four) uses the length of exchange three (4:11 by Cael's count) as if it were Brom's whole clock, though Chapter 51 says both clocks "started the moment the two of them walked out" and exchange one ran "most of two minutes". Either the clock is cumulative hard contact, in which case the number is wrong, or it restarted, in which case the earlier sentence is. A listener who has been doing the sums, as the chapter invites, will stop.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:44:Observation to keep: the whole exchange-four sequence (eleven seconds, four reasons it was not the end) is the clearest piece of fight-writing in the movement and should not be touched.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:65:- Gault, after trial four: "This wing measures six things. Five of them have moved and one hasn't." At that moment four trials have run; the cold runs have not. The sentence is true by the end of the sitting (board, read, combined, cold board, cold read moved; plate did not) but it is said before the instruments have said it, which is precisely the thing Gault would not do.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:102:| Action / suspense | 8 | Ch 52 "The fourth exchange lasted eleven seconds"; Ch 55 the four pieces | Trackable contest with named costs; earned length. Docked for the cumulative-clock wobble | High |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:115:- **Brom's clock.** Ch 51: both clocks "started the moment the two of them walked out"; Ch 51 end of exchange one: "His four minutes had begun"; Ch 52: "four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more" taken from exchange three alone. Three different start points for one clock.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-cold.md:145:- **Observed issue:** *eleven* carries roughly nineteen unrelated counts across six chapters. "Four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more" treats exchange three's duration as Brom's whole clock after Chapter 51 said both clocks started at the walk-out. The glance tally names six people and claims seven. The ledger says "Drifts: two" and "it never flickered" in one entry. Brom's strapped hand appears without a cause.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:2603:It stayed. It did not go out, the way the word had gone out. It sat there in the dark behind his breastbone, quiet and plain, in the way a figure sits on a page once it has been written down.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:2617:He sat on the cot for a long time with the notice there in the dark behind his breastbone, and did not write anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:2713:He blew out his small piece of the light by turning his face to the wall. He lay a long time with the notice quiet behind his breastbone and his hip aching, and listened to the district's late sounds come up through the window, and did not sleep for a while.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:2763:He had it with him. It was behind his breastbone, quiet and plain, in the dark place that was not quite as dark as it had been. *Wind-adjacent.* It was there every moment. It had been there at Vell's table and on the wall and in the gate, and it was there now in the lane. Every step he took beside her, it was there, and every step he did not say it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:2775:He did not know how long he could carry it. He knew it would not be long. He thought, walking home with his hip aching, that it might be two weeks, if he was careful, and that he did not want to be careful. He thought that the thing behind his breastbone was partly hers. He thought that every morning he kept it from her in the grey half, it would get heavier, the way a thing does that has been held up too long. Nothing that has to be held is free.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-39.md:55:"The leaf says the function is appended to the reading and advises what's entered. It doesn't say what happens when the reading gives it nothing to advise, and nothing else in the case says it in words." She looked at Cael. "But your file says it. The petition put it in schedule two by its full title, on the first night of the year, and you read it. *Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4.*"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-39.md:59:"Advisory, the same word, on a designation nobody at any height has ever been able to trace to an office." Karis drew a breath. "Cael told me on the third night, when he brought the bread. I asked him about Denvash, and he told me: eleven seconds. The plate lit eleven seconds late, and the word came at the end of them."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-39.md:63:"Eleven seconds is a long time for a reading," said Karis. "Every other reading on the continent is done before you've finished a breath. I think the function had his reading in front of it for eleven seconds and couldn't find a column to put it in, any column, and couldn't take the margin off because it was all margin. So it did what a good form does when it can't be filled in: it failed safe, and wrote the one word it had for a thing that couldn't be written. Then it marked the file, so that whoever came after would know there was something there it hadn't been able to correct." She laid the slip down. "The mark has no office behind it because no office made it. It made itself, the way a stamp comes down when a lever's pulled. And Ilsev sent it up, at the hearing, twice, to every height she could reach, and asked who'd authorized it. Something answered her each time, something that wasn't anybody."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-39.md:209:"I've thought about it every night this week, who you'd file it with. The seat runs on it, and so does the registry. Every evaluation office in the Compact sends its readings through it. You'd be filing a complaint about the corrections function with an office whose whole business is entering what the corrections function advises. And they'd read it, and they'd find nothing irregular in it, because there isn't anything irregular in it. Every form's been filled in properly for two hundred years." She took her hand off the notebook. "There isn't a seat outside it. There's nobody to send it to who isn't standing on it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-cold-prompt.md:1413:*Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-36.md:43:"*Memorandum to keepers of stations and to clerks of entry. Corrective classification at Kindling evaluation.*" She put her finger under the line on the newest leaf. "And the body. It's three sentences, and it's been three sentences since this one." She touched the yellowest. "A word changes here and there, and *shall* became *is to*. A clause about the post came in when the post did. Otherwise you could lay the oldest on top of the newest and read straight through them."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-36.md:97:"*Of the advisory corrections function. The function is appended to the reading and is not the reading. It does not alter what the reading shows. It advises what is to be entered, and the entry is made as advised. It is to be maintained, and its maintenance is the office's charge.*"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-36.md:119:He thought of Denvash, which he did not often let himself do. A district office on a cold morning, a chalk circle on boards worn into two shallow places where a generation of feet had stood, and a warden-adjunct with tired grey eyes three feet away at a desk with a brass plate let into it. Something had woken behind his breastbone, small, a point of light at the edge of his sight that he could feel and never point to. He had counted eleven seconds while the plate did not light, and then the word had come, very far away and very close, and the plate lighting late with the same word in it, and the light at the edge of his sight going out like a pinched wick.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-36.md:121:All his life since, he had said that his Arbiter had spoken once and gone dark. He had said it to panels and wardens and Magisters, and written it in two books. It had been the one fixed fact at the bottom of every argument he had ever won. It had read him once, and said one word, and the registry had written down that word because it had nothing else to write, and he lived in the gap the word left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-36.md:123:The leaf said there were two things in that office, not one. There was the reading, and there was something appended to it. And there had been eleven seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-42.md:73:Lira saw it too, a step later than he did. She stopped. She stood in a narrowing strip of honest wood with Fiske's slick on both sides of her and across her front, and every inch of the strip had been drawn, in eleven seconds, by a woman who knew exactly where Lira's feet liked to go and had simply removed all of those places before Lira got there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-37.md:15:He told the circle chalked on the worn boards of a district office, and the warden-adjunct three feet away watching the brass plate let into her desk, and the thing that woke behind his breastbone and came up to the edge of his sight. He told the eleven seconds he had counted while the plate did not light, and the one word that came at the end of them, very far away and very close, and the light at the edge of his sight going out like a pinched wick and never coming back when he looked. He told the letter that had made Denvash impossible for Hesk's sake, and the road east. He told Lira next, because Lira had come next: six weeks of bouts in a yard at Ardenmere, with her knocking him down on the boards between them more times than either of them had counted. Then one cold night on a cot under a window, with the Log on his knee, something had been written in the dark place behind his breastbone where the light had gone out.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-37.md:81:"No frame has ever read anything off me but what I put in front of it. The plates in the wing read what I give them, and I give them the band. The read at Brom's grade is a surface, and I can hold a surface. And my own Arbiter went out at Denvash after one word. It's never lit since. I've not stood in a station since."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/REPAIR-BRIEF.md:72:   started" and ch52's "four minutes of iron and eleven seconds more" agree.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-cold.md:108:**Reserved disclosures.** Vastin's three-sentence advisory is quoted whole in ch 6 ("You told us at Norhold there were three sentences … none of us had ever seen them"). "Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4" is cited and deliberately not argued from. The procurator's name is withheld from the reader (Bracken says it is unknown; the name itself is never printed). Whether any of these should have stayed reserved is plan adherence, not a canon finding, and I cannot judge it cold.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-35.md:203:"*Order of reclassification at evaluation. River station, the fourth district. Entry of the twelfth.*" He stopped, and found his place. "*Per corrective classification at Kindling evaluation: enter Current, Rank One. Margin reading not to be entered. Observe nine weeks following entry.*"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md:480:Cael counted it. He could not help counting it. From the moment the pen touched the first column to the moment it lifted from the second, eleven seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/compiled-prompt.md:482:He filed them where the other eleven lived. A circle of pale wood in an office at Denvash, on the morning of his Kindling, and a brass plate at Pellin's elbow that had stayed dark for eleven seconds before it lit, while a fourteen-year-old boy stood in the circle and did not breathe. He had thought then that eleven seconds was the longest any office would ever take to decide what he was.
