editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:2908:- Fragments: **none**. Arbiter: not yet woken. Functional level: none; a trained eye only.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:2977:**Fragments & progression.** Arbiter woke at Kindling; after the word it dimmed and settled at the edge of his sight; not consulted since. No declaration, no fragments, no notices. Capability: a trained eye (stances, tells); the unexamined cart-step (instinct only, unwritten — reserved for Lira's question in M2).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:2991:- The Arbiter's sigil goes dark after the word and does not answer when Cael looks for it (BOOK_MAP §1).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3017:**Fragments & progression.** None. Arbiter not consulted (dark since the word; no attempt staged — the courtyard is M3's). Circuit: **unrated, 0–1** (loss to Renn, Cu3 Blade, fourth exchange, by the flat, called). A return bout with Renn is requested at a month, "inclined to give it". **Instance count:** none logged. The Renn third exchange is filed "whole and unexamined", and the cart sits beside it uncounted ("he did not let himself count them, because counting them would have been the first step toward a word"). M3's sparring plant can be "first instance" as planned.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3098:- No fragments, no notices. The Arbiter is **dark**: absence, tested at length on the night of day 28.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3834:At age 14, every person undergoes Kindling: the moment their latent Path potential activates. Kindling is involuntary — it happens regardless of whether the person is ready. An **Arbiter** appears at the moment of Kindling: a small glowing sigil that only the Kindling person can see and hear. The Arbiter evaluates the person's internal architecture and assigns their Path classification.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3856:As a practitioner advances through ranks, new abilities manifest — presented by the Arbiter as visible ability declarations, experienced as text-like constructs in the practitioner's perception. These are called **Path declarations** and are specific to the practitioner's Path type.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3964:- **The line is sharp, not a gradient:** a stride inside, the Arbiter is dark and no declaration renders; a stride outside, it is back — practitioners describe the return as a clock resuming (Lira's clock). Every Arbiter in a party fails identically, at the same stride, one way and back the same, regardless of Path or tier (B7 Ch10–11, Ch18, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-40.md:91:*Four streets back from the seat, on the wharf side. The tall house with the brass plate. The third floor. The second bell after noon. Neither office's. Nothing written.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-40.md:111:The lane was narrow and steep, with a gutter down the middle and the backs of the warehouses on one side and a row of tall old houses on the other, let out floor by floor to clerks and factors and men who did a trade in paper. The building was the fourth along, with a door with a brass plate beside it listing its tenants, and a keeper's window, and a stair. Seln was at the keeper's window when Cael came in, writing his reason in the book, and did not look round.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-40.md:133:"He came in by the front, not the yard. He walked up the lane from the wharf end, on the gutter side, in grey, with nothing in his hands, and he stopped and read the brass plate by the door, and then he went in past the keeper's window, where the keeper could see him." Seln looked at the door. "By the clock on the landing, eleven minutes early."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:1159:*Return, from the chain of review, to the senior evaluation seat, on referral of the matter at Greyvane. Designation: Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-009/review-cold-prompt.md:633:He had not meant to. It was not in the plan; nothing borrowed was in the plan, and he and Lira had settled that on the first morning of the straw post without either of them having to say it. But it had been sitting in him since Feryn's wall like a question at the end of a page. There were two of them now, side by side in the dark behind his breastbone, the leaning one and the heavy one. He had only ever picked up one at a time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-009/review-cold-prompt.md:1151:He had not asked for it. There was no time to ask for anything, and he had not asked for it since the trough. It came up out of the dark behind his breastbone as it had come in the sleet, already done before he knew it was happening, and the yard was a hand's width narrower than it had been. His weight was not where his heel had been. It was round the edge of the blow, on Darrow's left, at an angle no step of his own could have got to from where he stood. The straight went through the space where his chest had been, close enough that he felt it go by along his shirt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-009/review-cold-prompt.md:1213:He would go back over it a great many times, on the cot, and in the grey half, and on the wall by the pump, and it never once came out with a choice in it. His weight was going round on the Wind, and it went further than the Wind went. And in the dark behind his breastbone, beside the leaning thing, the heavy one was there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-009/review-cold-prompt.md:1341:Cael felt the quiet all round him, and three hundred people inside it waiting to carry something home. He thought of the Log in his coat on the bench, open at last night's page. He thought of the line under *Evidence* with nothing after it but *Ruling*. He had filled that line in this afternoon, for the crossing. There was another line, under all of it, that had never had anything written beside it at all, since a word on a brass plate in Denvash, and there was nothing beside it now. Something in him had done a thing he could not describe. He had watched it happen from the inside, like a tenant watching the house he rents get up and walk.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-009/review-cold-prompt.md:1431:It came the way the others had come. There was the quiet first, the quiet before a thought arrives whole; then the turning over; then, in the dark place behind his breastbone where nothing had lit since the word, something written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:711:Every one of their chairs had a brass plate on its back with a name cut into it. He had read the plates from the floor with a borrowed glass on the first day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:723:*Every other chair in that row has a brass plate on its back. Twelve has a pale square where a plate used to be, two empty screw holes, a brushed seat, and a steward at the head of the stair. No name.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-006/compiled-prompt.md:1364:| Cael | Sixteen (turned on the eleventh of Sowing, Book 4; the date is never set beside a season word, OWNER #35). Healthy, rested, and trained: sixty-one floor sessions over the recess. No current injuries: B4 closed him fit (the quarter-burst's hip load ended the night of the twenty-third of Reaping; the plate's right-shoulder ache eased by the week's end). The leading hip carries the Wind fragment's old strain (crest to inner knee after a hard evening), and the landing beat is still unshortened. The right shoulder pays Pressure, "four blows a sitting", the circle's private cap and not a registry schedule (B4 ch62; OWNER #36: the plate/Pressure shoulder is the right). The Shadow fragment's rent runs from waking, spent or not; drifts come in the gaps, never in the work, and the weekly count is falling; the working ledger's day count since the stair and the protocol *Hold. First.* are the discipline. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
