editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/pre-repair-r2/chapter-06.md:67:All his life he had thought the watching was a kind of hiding, a way of standing a little outside things so that they could not quite reach him. He had thought he would have to grow out of it. He had counted eleven seconds in a worn circle. He had named what his own hands were doing on the morning of the notice instead of feeling it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-008/compiled-prompt.md:621:Nobody ever had. In a year of wardens and evaluators and brass plates and panels, everybody who looked at him had been looking for a line to fill in or a figure to post. Nothing in her face was going to be written down anywhere. She had come across something that was on none of her tables, and in front of eight thousand people she had stopped to find out what it was.
