editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/review-editorial-prompt.md:3916:- **The Copper final (developed; the series' best-matched bout since Cael–Brom).** Two clocks: Brom's hardening fades past about four minutes, and Lira has three bursts with the fourth "the one she told him about." **1:** she asks the seam three ways and the counter is *already there*; it isn't speed but a different skeleton. She grins. **2:** Brom takes it; Rooke taught him to *stop finishing the absorption*, eating a fifth of every strike; two bursts; she is put on the boards. **3 (four minutes eleven):** the least Lira-shaped thing she has ever done — walking backward around the floor twice on foot, *spending his clock*; the stretch to five beats; the third burst; heel behind the knee. **4 (eleven seconds):** he goes straight at the hip, no disguise. The fourth burst. She lands on the bad hip *on purpose* so the fold carries her during a beat that can't move. "She used a wound as a mechanism." He hauls her up; neither lets go for three seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:2603:It stayed. It did not go out, the way the word had gone out. It sat there in the dark behind his breastbone, quiet and plain, in the way a figure sits on a page once it has been written down.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:2617:He sat on the cot for a long time with the notice there in the dark behind his breastbone, and did not write anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:2713:He blew out his small piece of the light by turning his face to the wall. He lay a long time with the notice quiet behind his breastbone and his hip aching, and listened to the district's late sounds come up through the window, and did not sleep for a while.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:2763:He had it with him. It was behind his breastbone, quiet and plain, in the dark place that was not quite as dark as it had been. *Wind-adjacent.* It was there every moment. It had been there at Vell's table and on the wall and in the gate, and it was there now in the lane. Every step he took beside her, it was there, and every step he did not say it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:2775:He did not know how long he could carry it. He knew it would not be long. He thought, walking home with his hip aching, that it might be two weeks, if he was careful, and that he did not want to be careful. He thought that the thing behind his breastbone was partly hers. He thought that every morning he kept it from her in the grey half, it would get heavier, the way a thing does that has been held up too long. Nothing that has to be held is free.
