editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-54.md:185:Cael had looked at it every time he came into this room and had never once got a name for it. Squat, copper, three short legs, a little larger than two fists: that was the pot. Out of its lid stood a glass straw scored with lines as close as a comb's teeth. A small brass plate on its belly carried a date of calibration in paint, and the date was this month's. The clerk set it on its legs on the oak a pace from the crossing and stepped back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-009/pre-repair/chapter-56.md:53:He had not meant to. It was not in the plan; nothing borrowed was in the plan, and he and Lira had settled that on the first morning of the straw post without either of them having to say it. But it had been sitting in him since Feryn's wall like a question at the end of a page. There were two of them now, side by side in the dark behind his breastbone, the leaning one and the heavy one. He had only ever picked up one at a time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-40.md:265:It stayed. It did not go out, the way the word had gone out. It sat there in the dark behind his breastbone, quiet and plain, in the way a figure sits on a page once it has been written down.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-40.md:279:He sat on the cot for a long time with the notice there in the dark behind his breastbone, and did not write anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-40.md:375:He blew out his small piece of the light by turning his face to the wall. He lay a long time with the notice quiet behind his breastbone and his hip aching, and listened to the district's late sounds come up through the window, and did not sleep for a while.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-40.md:425:He had it with him. It was behind his breastbone, quiet and plain, in the dark place that was not quite as dark as it had been. *Wind-adjacent.* It was there every moment. It had been there at Vell's table and on the wall and in the gate, and it was there now in the lane. Every step he took beside her, it was there, and every step he did not say it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-40.md:437:He did not know how long he could carry it. He knew it would not be long. He thought, walking home with his hip aching, that it might be two weeks, if he was careful, and that he did not want to be careful. He thought that the thing behind his breastbone was partly hers. He thought that every morning he kept it from her in the grey half, it would get heavier, the way a thing does that has been held up too long. Nothing that has to be held is free.
