editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1104:"Your Kindling assessment," she said. "Standard process. Your Arbiter will resolve here, in front of the registry ledger." She tapped a flat brass plate set into the desktop at her elbow. It was about the size of a book, dull, unremarkable. "When your result reaches the Registry, this lights. I record what it shows. The process takes between three and fifteen minutes. Any questions before we begin?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1132:That was the first thing. None of the eleven descriptions on page seven had told him that. He had imagined something arriving, the way light arrives through a window. Instead, it gathered from inside him, from somewhere behind his breastbone, behind his sternum, as though it had always been there and had only now decided to be noticed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1138:He glanced at Pellin. She was three feet away, watching the brass plate. Her face showed nothing. She could not see it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1154:He watched Pellin's face from the corner of his eye. Her face was information. She was not looking at him. She was looking at the brass plate.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1184:He had been counting for eleven seconds. He was quite certain. He had counted every one.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1192:The brass plate at Pellin's elbow lit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1194:It was eleven seconds late. Text rose up in it, pale and even, and settled into the same word he had just heard.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1206:She did not say the word. Cael understood why, even then, standing in the circle with eleven seconds of silence still sitting in his chest. It was not unkindness. The word had already arrived. They both knew it. Saying it aloud would only have been for form, and she was not a person who did things for form.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1246:*Eleven seconds.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:1552:The seal was dark wax. The Compact's mark was pressed into it, a hand holding a balance. The pressing was so clean and even that a machine must have done it. Cael thought, for no good reason, of the brass plate on Pellin's desk. All this care, poured into the outside of things.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-001/review-editorial-prompt.md:2320:He thought about the eleven seconds, counting in the worn circle while the sigil hung at the edge of his sight. He thought about his own hands on the kitchen table the morning the notice came, and how he had looked at them and named what they were doing instead of feeling it. He thought about copying the archive entry word for word, in his neatest writing, so that he would not have to simply sit there and know it.
