editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/B5-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:271:B5 canon (ch60:109–129): "a room no window had ever been cut into"; the question *Whether the classification [SHATTERED] shall be designated an active threat category.*; Vastin's evidence (D17); "Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4" read in; "which office had authorized that designation. Nobody in the room could say."; the trace followed "to a sub-layer under the registry's own floor, and there lost … the attempt had been closed"; "a flag no living hand had authorized"; "Nobody called for a vote. The question was *entered for formal proceedings*."; no "four centuries" anywhere in ch54–60; the file "thicker by one entry with no number in it". M1:13 ("A room with no windows has 'entered for formal proceedings' a question about [SHATTERED]") holds. Note for M1:30 ("Nothing about … a sub-layer"): the word "sub-layer" is on B5's page once, in the narrator's window (ch60:125), known to nobody at Halcenvane — the rule stands; the instrument served in M1 may cite the designation by its full name, *Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4* (B4 ch49:17; B5 ch60:121), and carries nothing of the trace. B5 ch60:109 also says the sitting is known "from a few lines of its minute and from one participant's account, given late and to one person" — the plant is B5's; B6 owes it nothing on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair-r2/chapter-13.md:119:Cael counted it. He could not help counting it. From the moment the pen touched the first column to the moment it lifted from the second, eleven seconds.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/pre-repair-r2/chapter-13.md:121:He filed them where the other eleven lived. A circle of pale wood in an office at Denvash, on the morning of his Kindling, and a brass plate at Pellin's elbow that had stayed dark for eleven seconds before it lit, while a fourteen-year-old boy stood in the circle and did not breathe. He had thought then that eleven seconds was the longest any office would ever take to decide what he was.
