editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:744:He blew out his small piece of the light by turning his face to the wall. He lay a long time with the notice quiet behind his breastbone and his hip aching, and listened to the district's late sounds come up through the window, and did not sleep for a while.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:792:He had it with him, behind his breastbone, quiet and plain, in the dark place that was not quite as dark as it had been. *Wind-adjacent.* It had been there at Vell's table and on the wall and in the gate, and it was there now in the lane. Every step he took beside her, it was there, and every step he did not say it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/compiled-prompt.md:804:He did not know how long he could carry it, only that it would not be long. He thought, walking home with his hip aching, that it might be two weeks, if he was careful, and that he did not want to be careful, and that the thing behind his breastbone was partly hers. He thought that every morning he kept it from her in the grey half, it would get heavier, the way a thing does that has been held up too long. Nothing that has to be held is free.
