editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-001/pre-repair/chapter-05.md:79:"Dellenmoor. Standard. Research standing pending; the library committee writes to you. Brom. Standard. Ninth day, first bell, east hall; the Blade cohort wants a look at you. Lira. Transfer, re-certification. Copper bracket. You register for the ladder by the fourteenth or you start the season on the bottom rung and climb from there." He licked a finger and turned the page. "Cael. Assay-provision enrollment. Straight to the registrar. Assessment wing, ground floor, the door with the brass plate. He's cleared the whole morning, which he does not do, so go now and look at the view later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:81:He had been putting off this page for three days. Every night he had opened the back section and looked at the white paper under the last entry, and closed it again, because what he wanted to write was not a fact. Everything else in the back of the book was a fact. The cart was a fact; the drop was a fact; the notice, with its plain words in the dark behind his breastbone, was the plainest fact of all. What he wanted to write tonight was a guess, and he had told Lira once, on a step under a lantern, that guessing was how you wrote the wrong thing down and then trusted it because it was written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:97:The wheezing man had begun his long whistle by the door. Yeni's lamp was down to a bead, and when he looked up she had turned on her side with her face to the wall, which meant either that she was asleep or that she had decided to let him think so. He put the Log back on the shelf beside Hesk's leather book and lay down on his right side, the side that did not catch, and lay awake for some time with the hip aching and the dark place behind his breastbone quiet and a little less dark than it had been.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:175:If it was anybody, and not only Lira, then it was everybody. Everybody he had ever watched hard enough. Renn's figure. Dessa's patience. The kiln boy's held breath, Sarel's closing, Talis planting where he could not see him go, Corbin reading feet at the mark. The woman with the shoulder doing her six positions in the old man's yard, every evening for three months, while he walked past. Any of them might have left something behind in him, quietly, the way the lock had left its shape in the key, and it might be sitting there now in the dark behind his breastbone with no notice on it yet, waiting for the right moment to come up.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:241:He knew what he was looking for, this time, or he thought he did. He went to the dark place behind his breastbone, the place that was not quite as dark as it had been, and found the Wind there. He did not find a word or a picture, or anything he could have drawn; it was more a sort of leaning in the dark, a readiness, the shape the step had left when it went through him. It was the thing he reached for by the cot every night. He did not reach for it now. He went past it, carefully, as you go past a sleeping dog, and felt about in the dark beyond it for anything that was not Lira's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:403:He told her about the quiet before a thought. He told her about the dark place behind his breastbone where the sigil had gathered at Kindling, and had been dark ever since, and how it had still been dark, and how something had been written in it anyway. He opened the Log to the back, to the page where he had copied it, and turned it round on his knee so that she could read it, and she leaned forward on the bed and read it with her lips moving very slightly, the way she read the board.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:553:*The fifth was two weeks ago, on the thirty-ninth night of the six weeks, on my cot at Torvin's. Something came up where the Arbiter used to be, written in the dark. I'll copy it exactly, because you'd want it exact.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:1765:It came the way the first one had come, thirty-seven nights ago, on this cot. There was no sound and no light and no direction it came from; there was the quiet first, the quiet before a thought arrives whole, and then the turning over, and then, in the dark place behind his breastbone where nothing had lit since the word, something written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:1829:He closed the book and set it on the shelf beside Hesk's leather one. He lay down very carefully on his back, which was the only way left that did not hurt, and found that it hurt anyway. He lay looking at the beam with its old nail holes in the light of Yeni's lamp, and felt the two things sitting quietly side by side in the dark behind his breastbone, the one that leaned and the one that pressed, and listened to the wheezing man begin to whistle.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold-prompt.md:1943:He thought about two lines of figures in the dark behind his breastbone where there had been one. There were two doors, perhaps, where he had thought there was only one, and he did not know where either of them went, or which of them he had come through, or whether there were others in the dark he had not found yet. He did not know what Kestrel had been, or what Feryn's hand had been, or whether Lira's three months and Feryn's one second were the same thing at all.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:10:The weaknesses a straight read shows are not structural. They are, first, a repertoire of habits that recur so often a listener hears the author under the characters: the explanatory "the way a X does Y" simile 283 times in 60 chapters, "exactly" 208 times, the measured pause 194 times, and the number eleven, which has become a tic (228 hits in 53 chapters; carrel eleven, eleven weeks, eleven seconds, eleven questions and eleven days are canon, but eleven instruments, eleven swings, eleven feet, eleven minutes for the porters, eleven thumbnail marks, eleven crosses in a term and "Lira has done it eleven times" are the author reaching for the same number). Second, a soft stretch in M3 (ch15–18), where the counting study is told once in the shorthand and once more to the three, and a window-dense run in M7 (ch45, ch47, ch49, the last of them the longest chapter in the book at 6,809 words) in which Cael's own stakes pause for three cutaways. Third, a handful of continuity seams that a line pass closes: the ladder book holds "four hundred and twelve names" on day 28 when ch9 has the Copper column at sixty-five lines; Lira is "ten days on the top line" three days after she took it, with a hip that was back in hall one on a day that has not happened yet; the Crown yard floor is dressed stone in ch6 and oak in every bout fought on it; Seln has six hands in ch14 and four everywhere after; ch34 reads rule two aloud in words the minute never used; the Iron read and Brom's acquaintance are "three years" old in M2–M3 where the ledger's canon is two; and the baseline is "the first month" seventeen times against the forty-eighth day. Sixty-eight line fixes below; three cross-movement priorities for one same-author pass in two lanes. Nothing needs a rebuild.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:22:The standings notation is kept as ruled: "six bouts unbeaten, none lost" (ch25), "nine bouts unbeaten, none lost, the opening bout drawn by lot among them" (ch29), Bracken's "Ten bouts unbeaten. None lost." written and read to "Eleven" at the ceremony (ch52). Lira's climb adds up: the drawn bout against Nyle (eleven seconds, three exchanges, exactly four bursts), five climbs of four places from twenty-second to the second line in ten sessions, the Shield fifth-year (forty-one wins; four bursts in eight seconds), the Current fourth-year (nine minutes, two bursts and one), the Fiske bout (even / Fiske / Lira with four bursts and the half-step / Lira), the semifinal (Fiske / Lira at the word / even / Lira onto the oil, two bursts), the final (even on the guard / Iron Skin / Wind at four minutes eleven / Wind in eleven seconds on the bad hip). Brom: Merrick 3–2 in the fifth by not turning; Tarn 2–3 on the fifth feed by the heel; Merrick 3–2 in the fifth by timing the pane; the nineteen four a week from the Tarn bout with the first four in one night, nine on d144, thirteen on the night of d149, seventeen on d156, round two from d157, exercise seven on d172, one a night from his semifinal to the eighteenth, round three for the recess. The brackets: 91 Copper, 63 Iron, 19 Silver, 173 names, twenty-one returners, Lira twenty-second by Rank Two, twenty-three shut out below sixty-eighth. The eight-and-four of the first morning (209 + 138 + 51 + 14 = 412) holds everywhere except ch10, below. The baseline (six on the board with the sixth wide; eleven of twelve with the ninth to the frame; seven of eight at the third weight; the plate four, low; twelve of twelve cold) is laid against the evaluation line for line (eight on the board, ceiling six; the vessel four times; eleven of twelve at the fourth weight; the plate four, low, unchanged; trial five void and eight of nine on the reserve; cold board a palm short and the read twelve of twelve). The glance tally, the fame tally (29 of 91; 9 of 14, 5 of 11, 7 of 19, 0 of 31), the nine dots, the five pen marks, the eleven questions in twenty-nine minutes, the sixteen seals, the four hands and the fifth, the four chests, the six filings, the four carbons, the forty-one pages and the eleven clauses of article forty-one, the two certified copies four hundred miles apart with three spelling differences on document eleven: all agree with themselves and with the ledger.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:50:2. **The number eleven** — 228 / 53 (ch10 fourteen, ch31 twelve, ch53 eight; seven each in ch11, ch12, ch20, ch28, ch56). Canon elevens stay: carrel eleven, eleven weeks, eleven seconds, eleven questions, eleven names on the manifest, eleven days, eleven of twelve, eleven hundred seats, eleven clauses of the committee's charter, Ilsev's eleven minutes and eleven months, Gault's eleven years, the eleven supervisors, the eleven rumours. The rest are reached for: eleven instruments, eleven Paths "never been close to", eleven swings at the bag, eleven feet on the stair, eleven minutes for the porters, eleven thumbnail marks, eleven crosses in a term, eleven years of indexes, eleven provision files, "eleven more chairs", "Lira has done it eleven times", eleven wins in Bracken's files for Nyle, eleven minutes for the supersession, eleven minutes for Withrow's address. Cut a third of them in each lane.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:366:1. **Thin the simile, pause and number repertoire (both lanes, every chapter).** Items 1–10 of §3 and the small verbatim repeats under them. Scope: one reading pass, sentence by sentence, no script; cap "the way a X does Y" and "as if / as though" together at three per chapter and never two on one gesture; cut "exactly", "for a long moment" and "without a word" where the sentence stands without them; let "did not look up" belong to Prynn and Bracken again; vary or drop the "He wrote it that night" frame around the Log while keeping the entries; explain the stake and the corner once in lane B and not in every chapter after; and take the number eleven out wherever it is not canon (lane A: eleven instruments, eleven Paths, eleven swings, eleven feet, Nyle's eleven wins; lane B: eleven minutes for the porters, eleven thumbnail marks, eleven crosses, eleven years of indexes, eleven provision files, "eleven more chairs", "Lira has done it eleven times", the supersession's eleven minutes), so that the elevens that matter — carrel eleven, eleven weeks, eleven seconds, eleven questions, eleven days, Ilsev's eleven minutes — ring. The first instance of each figure stays; the rest are rewritten in the character's own register or cut. Expect to lose two to three thousand words across the book and to get the characters back by ear.
