editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-22.md:29:"Denvash," he had said, and stopped, because that was enough. Every one of them knew the brass plate.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-10.md:49:*Every person who has ever decided a thing about me had a face, and I could read it. Pellin at Denvash, with her brass plate. Coss across a desk. Vastin with his frames. The provost who was frightened and couldn't hide it. Umber polishing his spectacles over a sheet he couldn't score. I read every one of them from across a room, and every reading was worth something.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-cold.md:13:**Am I oriented, arriving at chapter 41 mid-book?** Mostly yes, and faster than I expected. Within the first two pages I had: a boy (Cael, fourteen) at a boarding house (Torvin's) practising a borrowed move at night; a Log with a "back section" for things he cannot explain; a teacher (Lira, Wind Path) and a dawn yard ("the grey half"); a yard-keeper (Vell) with a book and a circle; and a strange notice that was "written in the dark" behind his breastbone. The chapter re-grounds those without ever stopping to explain. What I was *not* oriented on and simply carried as open tokens: Hesk (a mentor in Denvash with a workshop and a kitchen table), Kindling and the Arbiter (some declaration ceremony that failed him), Pellin's office and "the word", "the six weeks" and "the forty-second day", "the man with the pin", "the summons", "the Compact", "Coss", "Weaver's Row". A long roster of past opponents (Renn, Brenna, Petra, Dellin, Dessa, Talis, Corbin, Sarel, the cook) is name-dropped in lists (lines 175, 829). I never lost the thread because of them, but the lists are the one place a mid-book reader feels the weight of what they missed. The bracketed token `[SHATTERED]` (lines 955, 1617) reads to a cold reader as a redaction placeholder rather than a word a character says; I understood that it is the boy's tier and that it frightens people, and that is enough to work, but the brackets jolt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-001/compiled-prompt.md:1259:| Cael | Sixteen (turned on the eleventh of Sowing, Book 4; the date is never set beside a season word, OWNER #35). Healthy, rested, and trained: sixty-one floor sessions over the recess. No current injuries: B4 closed him fit (the quarter-burst's hip load ended the night of the twenty-third of Reaping; the plate's right-shoulder ache eased by the week's end). The leading hip carries the Wind fragment's old strain (crest to inner knee after a hard evening), and the landing beat is still unshortened. The right shoulder pays Pressure, "four blows a sitting", the circle's private cap and not a registry schedule (B4 ch62; OWNER #36: the plate/Pressure shoulder is the right). The Shadow fragment's rent runs from waking, spent or not; drifts come in the gaps, never in the work, and the weekly count is falling; the working ledger's day count since the stair and the protocol *Hold. First.* are the discipline. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-001/compiled-prompt.md:1302:- **Functional level:** Iron-equivalent in every evaluation. The registry sees [SHATTERED], unclassified, with the Suppression-Advisory Watch Level 4 (origin: registry sub-layer; authorizing office untraceable).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:21:| 13 | The Hand | 6,000 | 6 | **Day 35, Karis spends the budget**: certified copies of the founders' signature leaves from Greyvane; "before the midyear recess"; three lines left blank; "It's terrible. I've never been so careful in my life." The assistant's fourth error: **"Find it."** / "Yes." **Ephram and Brom at the old frames**, four evenings, **wordless** (the reset watched, the entry watched, the look at the end). **Day 39, the annex**: "Tomorrow is a form… Watch the seal." **Day 40, the first sitting**: thirty-one on the steps; the side-door officer with a cold; the list; **door log: *Caelen Hesk-ward* / *the enrollee of record, unclassified* — eleven seconds**, filed beside Pellin's brass plate; lot numbers in the floor (seventeen under his foot); five covered evaluation chairs; **the hooded seat** — hands, procedure, no name; Seln at the gallery's sightline seat. **HAVEL** (~1.24k): rotation sheet; the junior chair laid out by the manual; the door log checked; does not look (Greyvane's two looks); the times (nine minutes, twenty-three); **the seal ordinary**; the five sheets at the inn, the mark he was told to leave; **a sixth would need a fact — none**; reads all five, writes nothing. **Withrow bows anyway**; coach: the counsel, Karis ("To a seal"), Brom (Havel looked twice at Greyvane; "I counted"), Lira, **Seln's three grades**. Log: **"I keep looking for the person and finding the hand."** **Day 42, the month's close**: four slips on the sill (one blank); **"Whatever this challenge costs me, it should not cost them."**; Karis reads over his shoulder: **"That is not how any of us are built."**; the parenthesis verbatim; **be afraid of it accurately** — dates, a column, a total; a ruled column with four names, left empty. |
