editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-002/review-cold.md:178:- *Strength to preserve:* the officer with a cold and the eleven seconds; the hands that do only what procedure asks; the Havel interlude with its clean seal and no sixth sheet; Brom's "I counted"; and Seln's "It used to sit at the other table."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:81:He had been putting off this page for three days. Every night he had opened the back section and looked at the white paper under the last entry, and closed it again, because what he wanted to write was not a fact. Everything else in the back of the book was a fact. The cart was a fact; the drop was a fact; the notice, with its plain words in the dark behind his breastbone, was the plainest fact of all. What he wanted to write tonight was a guess, and he had told Lira once, on a step under a lantern, that guessing was how you wrote the wrong thing down and then trusted it because it was written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:97:The wheezing man had begun his long whistle by the door. Yeni's lamp was down to a bead, and when he looked up she had turned on her side with her face to the wall, which meant either that she was asleep or that she had decided to let him think so. He put the Log back on the shelf beside Hesk's leather book and lay down on his right side, the side that did not catch, and lay awake for some time with the hip aching and the dark place behind his breastbone quiet and a little less dark than it had been.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:175:If it was anybody, and not only Lira, then it was everybody. Everybody he had ever watched hard enough. Renn's figure. Dessa's patience. The kiln boy's held breath, Sarel's closing, Talis planting where he could not see him go, Corbin reading feet at the mark. The woman with the shoulder doing her six positions in the old man's yard, every evening for three months, while he walked past. Any of them might have left something behind in him, quietly, the way the lock had left its shape in the key, and it might be sitting there now in the dark behind his breastbone with no notice on it yet, waiting for the right moment to come up.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:241:He knew what he was looking for, this time, or he thought he did. He went to the dark place behind his breastbone, the place that was not quite as dark as it had been, and found the Wind there. He did not find a word or a picture, or anything he could have drawn; it was more a sort of leaning in the dark, a readiness, the shape the step had left when it went through him. It was the thing he reached for by the cot every night. He did not reach for it now. He went past it, carefully, as you go past a sleeping dog, and felt about in the dark beyond it for anything that was not Lira's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:403:He told her about the quiet before a thought. He told her about the dark place behind his breastbone where the sigil had gathered at Kindling, and had been dark ever since, and how it had still been dark, and how something had been written in it anyway. He opened the Log to the back, to the page where he had copied it, and turned it round on his knee so that she could read it, and she leaned forward on the bed and read it with her lips moving very slightly, the way she read the board.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:553:*The fifth was two weeks ago, on the thirty-ninth night of the six weeks, on my cot at Torvin's. Something came up where the Arbiter used to be, written in the dark. I'll copy it exactly, because you'd want it exact.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:1765:It came the way the first one had come, thirty-seven nights ago, on this cot. There was no sound and no light and no direction it came from; there was the quiet first, the quiet before a thought arrives whole, and then the turning over, and then, in the dark place behind his breastbone where nothing had lit since the word, something written.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:1829:He closed the book and set it on the shelf beside Hesk's leather one. He lay down very carefully on his back, which was the only way left that did not hurt, and found that it hurt anyway. He lay looking at the beam with its old nail holes in the light of Yeni's lamp, and felt the two things sitting quietly side by side in the dark behind his breastbone, the one that leaned and the one that pressed, and listened to the wheezing man begin to whistle.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:1943:He thought about two lines of figures in the dark behind his breastbone where there had been one. There were two doors, perhaps, where he had thought there was only one, and he did not know where either of them went, or which of them he had come through, or whether there were others in the dark he had not found yet. He did not know what Kestrel had been, or what Feryn's hand had been, or whether Lira's three months and Feryn's one second were the same thing at all.
