editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-009/review-editorial-prompt.md:551:The farthest broke first. In the outer court the people who could not get in had been following the bout from a man on a barrel at the mouth of the east tunnel, who could see a slice of the floor and called it out to them, exchange by exchange, as a crier calls a race. He had called the lane. He had got as far as *and the boy —* and then stopped, with the whole court looking up at him, for eleven seconds by a carter's count. When they shouted at him to go on he said he was sorry, he had run out of sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-009/review-editorial-prompt.md:1123:"If I gave you names I would be guessing, and I don't guess." He did not say it to be clever. He said it as Gault said a plate would not read past its last notch. "I can tell you what my year has looked like from my chair. A year ago I was asked what you are. This year I am asked what can be done about you. I answer every one of those letters by saying, again, what you are. Each answer goes up the stair. Each one is entered and filed. I am fairly sure none of them is read." He turned his left hand over, and back. "My office still works. It works very well. It has simply stopped mattering. When the questions stop being questions, an evaluator knows the decision has been taken in some room he was not shown."
