editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-004/compiled-prompt.md:450:"It came up the way everybody says. From behind here." He touched his breastbone. "It sat at the edge of my eye for eleven seconds. Then it said the word, and then it went out, like a lamp when you pinch the wick. And it hasn't come back." He made himself say the next part. "I didn't look for it again for four weeks. I was afraid to. Last night I went down into Torvin's yard at midnight and tried. Properly. I don't know how many times. I stopped counting."
