editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/pre-repair-r2/chapter-22.md:51:So he had gone to the start. A woman at Denvash with a brass plate on her desk that sat dark for eleven seconds before it lit; a name stamped on a card; a fourteen-year-old put out of the back door with nothing written down anywhere that said she had been wrong. Three years to get one sentence on paper that undid her.
