editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-48.md:107:Eight was cleaner than seven; he had expected it to be worse. Nine went through him at the right angle and still left the place behind his breastbone ringing like a struck pan.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-22.md:181:Since his Kindling he had not had one day without somebody writing him down. Assessors, a panel, an Arbiter with a classification, a warden with a challenge in his pocket, and a semester evaluation waiting at the end of this one; grey coats at every gate and ferry on two roads; and now a whole hill that had bought his transcript at six silver marks a copy and read it before he walked through the gate. He had grown so used to it that he only noticed it now in the way a man notices his own coat when somebody else asks him to take it off.
