editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-004/review-cold.md:7:**Orientation, arriving mid-book:** oriented within two pages. By the end of the first scene of 21 I know: Cael, fourteen, thirty-six days into Ardenmere after something at "Weaver's Row"/"Kindling" where a brass plate failed to light and left him with a word in square brackets on his card; the Compact (hand-and-balance pin) is the authority he is hiding from; Torvin's is his lodging; Hesk is the guardian he writes to in Denvash; Lira is the friend who trains him; the Cinder House yard is a fight circuit with a ledger kept by Vell; he has lost to Renn, Brenna, Amrit and Petra. The Log's front/back split and the *h* hearsay mark are explained in use. Things I did not understand and did not need to: "Garrik says the arm's still running clean"; "Tuesdays and the file"; what exactly the bracketed word says. Those read as earned earlier context, not as gaps.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-07.md:139:There was a case of glass on a stone plinth along one wall, and in it three crowns on three dark cushions with a brass plate under each. The Copper was the plainest of them, and the darkest, and worn bright along its top edge where a great many hands had lifted it. Its plate had been lengthened twice with new brass riveted on below the old.
