editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-002/review-cold-prompt.md:719:Cael thought about Pellin's office, the circle of pale wood, the brass plate that lit eleven seconds late. He thought about a form drawn from the back of a drawer, filled in with small quick strokes, and how nobody in that room had asked him anything, because there had not been anything to ask; the question had already been answered by someone who was not in the room.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-004/recheck-r1.md:18:- Ch22 still carries Denvash's eleven seconds, the ordered receipt list, Lira's floor argument, Cael's cost-free *Both roads*, Seln's two looks, the maintenance-record discovery/late corridor understanding, and the “wrong question / who decided” turn in their source-shaped local units.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-06.md:9:He found four other lines like it, once he started looking. A note about the hollow behind his breastbone sat at the bottom of a page about Ulric's heel. A line about the giving face of the Pressure, which had taken a Copper formal's guard down like a door off its hinges in a hot week, was jammed into the margin of a page about Dace's rings. One of Lira's sentences about the lock was in both books, in slightly different words, and he could not now remember which he had written first, or which was nearer to what she had actually said. That last one bothered him most. He had told himself, when he bought the slim book, that it would never hold a word it had not earned. And here was a sentence of Lira's living in two places in two shapes, so that if he ever needed to stand on it he would not know which of them would hold his weight.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-004/compiled-prompt.md:555:*Wind. Copper.* On a door in the second quadrangle. Eleven seconds, eight hundred people, a Stone Path on his back.
