editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-19.md:229:And it was not silence. He knew that now, standing in the yard, as clearly as he had known it in the side room. Silence would have been something. Silence would have been a thing that was there and was choosing not to answer, the way Pellin's brass plate had sat dark for eleven seconds and then lit. He could have waited out a silence. He could have knocked louder.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-003/pre-repair/chapter-19.md:247:Every one of them could reach into the dark behind their breastbone and find a light there, and the light would tell them what they were. Not all of it. Not the whole of a person. But the part that the city cared about. The part that decided which side of the bridge you slept on. Tier. Rank. Path. Whether you were getting better.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-003/review-editorial.md:90:- **Lira's cutaway** knows only what she saw: his hand going to the strap of a bag he was not carrying (she does not know the cart); Renn's third exchange from the rope; the drop. Her academy story stays as source gives it ("what you have done does not count because nobody approved it first"). No family, no life before the academy, no romance — what she wants is to be right about the skipped middle "in somebody else's body" and a partner who makes her better ✓. She has read the four-line summary (Tier A text quoted exactly in part) ✓ and does not know his Arbiter is dark until ch 20 ✓ (ch 18: "She wondered, for the first time, what his said about this morning" — consistent with her ch 20 surprise).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:1111:On the corner of the fish market there was a public house with two doors. The front one was propped open on a room full of wharfmen and smoke. The other, round the side, was shut, with a small brass plate screwed to it at the height of a man's eyes. Cael stopped and read the plate. It said that the back room was kept for ranked custom, and it gave the rank in a form of words that the registry had stopped using before Cael was born. Nobody had changed the plate. Nobody had needed to. Everybody who used that door knew what it meant.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/review-editorial-prompt.md:2864:| Cael | Sixteen (turned on the eleventh of Sowing, Book 4; the date is never set beside a season word, OWNER #35). Healthy, rested, and trained: sixty-one floor sessions over the recess. No current injuries: B4 closed him fit (the quarter-burst's hip load ended the night of the twenty-third of Reaping; the plate's right-shoulder ache eased by the week's end). The leading hip carries the Wind fragment's old strain (crest to inner knee after a hard evening), and the landing beat is still unshortened. The right shoulder pays Pressure, "four blows a sitting", the circle's private cap and not a registry schedule (B4 ch62; OWNER #36: the plate/Pressure shoulder is the right). The Shadow fragment's rent runs from waking, spent or not; drifts come in the gaps, never in the work, and the weekly count is falling; the working ledger's day count since the stair and the protocol *Hold. First.* are the discipline. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
