editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-45.md:61:He sat with the notebook open and did not believe a word of it. A rank was what an examiner could see in a hall on a given day, and he knew what that was worth: an Arbiter had once looked at him for eleven seconds and written down a single word.
