editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-005/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:28:| 33 | Section Twelve | 4,957 | **The walking channel**: *is there anybody*, yes/no only, thirty paces. **Kindled or not**: Brom's test at the dray, "a second coin under the first". **Working or resting**: the girl with sacking in her hair. **Lira asks Brom whether she is really past Copper (E11)**: her feet are past it; her hands (the turn from catch to send) are Copper still. "He told me where… I can work on a place." **HAVEL CUTAWAY (≈3,290).** The quarter's review sheet; box six, *Handling markers confirmed against manual*, gives him a reason. The supervisor's loans book; the index of designations: ***Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4***. Section Twelve: Gold tier and above, under active security review, with signature, date and review date required. The monitoring table, which nobody has ever applied to this file. Two drafts: the first ("cannot be correct… who entered it") pocketed to burn; the second sent. The same-afternoon reply verbatim (§8 item 25). Box six annotated *Queried; instructed per contact of record*. The notebook entry and two questions "the slip could not reach". The first draft burned at home, *who* last. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/state/movement-005/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:319:   - The record window goes from the shelved file directly to the line, still named in full (*Suppression-Advisory Watch, Priority Level 4*): no officer, no date, no renewal. Then the index, *systemic protocol, origin: registry sub-layer*, and the earlier date.
